# hexboot — Spring Boot Hexagonal Microservices
# Full instructions: ~/.claude/skills/hexboot/SKILL.md or .opencode/skills/hexboot/SKILL.md

<hexboot_workflows>
- CREATE: Ask developer for options (package, DB, security, etc.) → scaffold hexagonal project
- MODIFY: Detect existing hexagonal structure → add entity/endpoint/adapter
- MIGRATE: Convert Controller-Service-Repository → Hexagonal (10 steps)
- AUDIT: 22+ grep-based checks with severity and exact fix
</hexboot_workflows>

<hexboot_rules>
- domain/ must have ZERO framework imports (Spring, JPA, Jackson)
- @Transactional goes on application use case, NOT domain or adapter
- @PreAuthorize goes on inbound port interface, NOT on controller
- Layer dependency: domain ← application ← adapter (never the reverse)
- Domain model = pure Java, JPA entity = separate class in adapter
- Naming: Order (domain), OrderEntity (JPA), OrderResponse (DTO), OrderMapper
</hexboot_rules>

<hexboot_audit>
- Architecture scan: 12 checks (grep-based)
- Optimization scan: 5 checks (N+1, indexes, transactions, blocking, cache)
- Production-readiness: 10 checks (actuator, secrets, Docker, MDC, error codes)
- Security scan: 4 checks (@PreAuthorize placement, CSRF, SecurityChain)
- Test coverage: 3 checks
</hexboot_audit>
